## Results: TAM / TAX / LDR-final (2026-07 readouts)

- TAM (text-derived per-class diagonal metric): **48.73 -- best number of
  the entire project.** +0.56 over base try1 (48.17) on PLAIN PARSeg3 (no
  LCR), above the LCR band (48.60/48.48). First text win after five
  failures/neutrals.
  Why it (probably) worked where others died -- fits the surviving design
  law exactly: zero-init identity start (w==1 -> byte-identical PARSeg3 at
  t=0), zero new losses, tiny bounded change (0.5*tanh), and the text role
  is METRIC STRUCTURE (which channels matter per class; shared projection
  W couples metric updates across description-similar classes) rather than
  class-identity geometry (the cone-fatal role).
  MANDATORY control before this goes in the thesis: TAM-NT (no-text
  variant, w = 1 + 0.5*tanh(r) only) decides whether LANGUAGE content is
  load-bearing or any learned per-class diagonal metric suffices.
- TAX (language-anchored deep supervision): trending well below 48 ->
  judged failed. Inverse of prior expectation (TAX was rated the safer of
  the pair): text at backbone mid-features via disposable aux = no; text
  as inference-time metric structure (TAM) = yes.
- LDR final (owner reported as "lrp", read as LDR): best 47.15 over the
  whole run -- confirms the 88k kill.
- Subsequent owner-reported finals: TDL 47.66; LTM 48.21. Detailed
  interpretation is recorded in the LTM follow-up section below. TAM-NT
  remains unreported.
- Text scorecard update: LTA -1.2 / PTA -1.2 / LTC ~0 / PAT ~0 /
  LDR -1.0 / TAX fail / **TAM +0.56 WIN** / ACT +0.38* /
  TDL **47.66 (-0.51, FAIL)** / LTM **48.21 (+0.04, FLAT)**.

