## RABA mask-classification route: FAILED (final read-outs, 2026-07-21)

- RABA changed the decision paradigm from PARSeg3's dense pixel classifier
  to region-query mask classification with learned class centers and four
  routed attribute residuals. It remained end-to-end, text-free, and used
  the same EfficientFormerV2-S2 backbone / ADE20K 160k protocol.
- Original RABA (3 decoder layers, final-stage loss only): `43.05` at 80k,
  versus same-stage PARSeg3 `46.32`. The run was stopped as badly
  under-optimized.
- RABA-3L with all-stage auxiliary supervision: **46.38 final**.
- RABA-6L with all-stage auxiliary supervision: **46.95 final**.
- Deep supervision rescued optimization, while 3L -> 6L added `+0.57`;
  nevertheless the best variant remains `-1.22` versus the current
  PARSeg3 try1 reference (`48.17`) and `-1.89` versus the separately
  reported stronger PARSeg3 asset (`48.84`).
- Decision: close RABA as the main line. Do not spend slots on A=1, 9-layer
  depth, or HyperConnection controls: the route is already noncompetitive,
  and its surviving gain is attributable to generic decoder depth rather
  than the proposed multi-attribute decision mechanism.

