## Reference tables (owner-supplied, 2026-07-27) -- USE THESE FOR ALL COMPARISONS

OffSeg paper (ICCV 2025, Table 2; FLOPs @512x512 for ADE20K):
  OffSeg-T  6.2M   5.3G   ADE20K 44.2   Cityscapes 78.9   COCO-Stuff 41.9
  OffSeg-B  13.0M  10.3G  ADE20K 45.9   Cityscapes 80.5   COCO-Stuff 44.3
  OffSeg-L  26.4M  17.1G  ADE20K 48.5   Cityscapes 81.6   COCO-Stuff 46.0

Senior's PARSeg table (* = his own OffSeg reproduction, not the paper number):
  OffSeg-T 6.22M  9.54G  43.75*  ->  PARSeg-T 8.98M  17.92G  45.25   (+1.50)
  OffSeg-B 12.96M 14.88G 46.08*  ->  PARSeg-B 15.71M 23.26G  48.84   (+2.76)
  OffSeg-L 26.41M 22.09G 48.49*  ->  PARSeg-L 29.17M 30.47G  49.67   (+1.18)
  Increase is CONSTANT across scales: +2.75M params, +8.38G FLOPs.

Notes:
- +2.75M confirms the independent estimate of the PARSeg branch cost
  (2 x 1800 x 256 queries = 0.92M, FFN 256<->2048 = 1.05M, attention +
  projections + proto/route/AGCF). The branch is backbone-independent, which
  is why the delta is identical at T/B/L; it pays off most at B (+2.76).
- FLOPs conventions differ between the two tables (OffSeg-B 10.3G vs 14.88G),
  so FLOPs must be compared WITHIN one table only.
- Owner ruling on baselines: take the LOWER of {paper, reproduction} as the
  reference. For ADE20K-B that is 45.9 (paper), not 46.08 (senior's repro).
- CAVEAT ON FILE: this repo reproduces PARSeg-B at 48.17, i.e. 0.67 BELOW the
  senior's 48.84, so this environment appears to run systematically low. An
  environment-matched OffSeg-B would therefore likely land below 45.9-46.08,
  which would make our own deltas LARGER, not smaller. Never measured.

## Own-decoder line (generation series): OffSeg + our own second stage

Motivation: every one of the ~30 previous attempts was "PARSeg3 + X" and is
therefore structurally disqualified for the thesis (high overlap with the
senior's work, small delta). This line inherits ONLY OffSeg (legitimately
shared with the senior) and replaces the entire PARSeg3 second stage --
attribute decoder, prototype calibration, routing, AGCF, +2.75M / +8.38G --
with our own mechanism.

- OffSeg-CCM (gen 1, T=1, rank 64, 0.11M): **46.8 final.**
  vs OffSeg-B 45.9 = +0.9, i.e. ~40% of the senior's +2.27..+2.76 at ~1/25 of
  the parameters.
  Needle acc_ccm_gain converged to **0.20** against a tanh bound of 1.0 -> the
  conditional metric IS used (zero-init gate pushed up and held), and the
  output bound is NOT the limit; raising ccm_gain_scale would do nothing.
  The predicted failure mode (context degenerating to a single class vector
  late, driving gain to 0) did NOT occur.
  Tail: 128k 46.65 / 144k 46.57 / 160k 46.79 -- FLAT, unlike LCR whose
  endpoint was its peak. The mechanism saturated.
- OffSeg-CCM2 (gen 2, T=3 fixed point + rank 192, 0.19M): RUNNING.
- OffSeg-CCM2-T1 (capacity-only control, T=1 + rank 192): RUNNING in parallel.
  The three points decompose gen 2 into iteration effect vs capacity effect,
  which decides generation 3.

