## New probe added this round

- tools/probe_boundary_snap_oracle.py -- splits the boundary oracle into
  relocatable vs semantic. Result (2000 val images, base 48.17):
    band r=3: FULL +11.52 | SNAP@R=16 +4.01 (49.0% of band errors relocatable)
    band r=5: FULL +16.41 | SNAP@R=16 +4.54 (41.3%)
    band r=8: FULL +21.99 | SNAP@R=16 +4.38 (31.8%)
  The FULL oracle scales with band width (it only measures how much of the
  image is handed over); the SNAP oracle is FLAT across band widths, which is
  why +4.5 is the number to design against. At R=4 (a short-reach offset
  field) it is only +2.32 / +1.30 / +0.44.

